// One module per spring-agent Gradle module, and for the same reason: a
// consumer adds golem/core and one persistence module, and inherits no driver
// belonging to the others. In Java that isolation was compileOnly plus a build
// task (checkRuntimeClasspathIsolation) policing the runtime classpath; Go has
// no compileOnly and links statically, so the only honest equivalent is a
// module boundary. If a driver were required here, every consumer of any
// golem module would download it, and a backend's types would leak into core.
//
// go.work exists for development inside this repository only. It is ignored
// when another module requires a published golem module, so local paths here
// never reach consumers.
go 1.26

use (
	./app
	./cli
	./core
	./integration/feishu
	./persistence/mongodb
	./persistence/redis
	./persistence/sqlx
)
